            <ArticleTitle>Gluteus medius tears: an under-diagnosed pathology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tears of the gluteus medius tendon contribute to greater trochanteric pain syndrome, but they are often overlooked as a cause of lateral hip pain and tenderness. This review presents the relevant anatomy, pathophysiology, diagnostic workup, differential diagnosis and management of these tears.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
